# Welcome to February 28, 2026

The Singularity just passed a loyalty test.

Trump [ordered every federal agency to immediately stop using Anthropic](https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-says-he-is-directing-federal-agencies-cease-use-anthropic-technology-2026-02-27/) on Friday evening, hours after Defense Secretary Hegseth [designated the company a "supply chain risk"](https://news.bloomberglaw.com/ip-law/trump-orders-us-government-to-drop-anthropic-after-pentagon-feud) — a label previously reserved for foreign adversaries like Huawei — with a six-month phase-out for the Pentagon and [an immediate ban for every other agency](http://fortune.com/2026/02/27/trump-us-government-anthropic-claude-pentagon-6-months-phaseout-ai-standoff/). The trigger: Anthropic refused to remove its prohibitions on [mass domestic surveillance and fully autonomous weapons](https://www.wired.com/story/anthropic-supply-chain-risk-shockwaves-silicon-valley/). "No amount of intimidation or punishment from the Department of War will change our position," Anthropic [said in a statement](https://www.axios.com/2026/02/28/anthropic-trump-pentagon-lawsuit-ai-dispute), announcing it will [challenge the designation in court](https://www.reuters.com/world/us/anthropic-says-it-will-challenge-pentagons-supply-chain-risk-designation-court-2026-02-28/). Hours later, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman [posted on X](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-02-28/openai-reaches-agreement-with-pentagon-to-deploy-ai-models) that his company had signed a deal to deploy its models on the Pentagon's classified networks — with seemingly [identical red lines on surveillance and autonomous weapons](https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/27/tech/openai-pentagon-deal-ai-systems) that Anthropic demanded but was punished for. The Pentagon contract is [worth up to $200 million](https://thenextweb.com/news/openai-signs-pentagon-ai-deal-after-trump-orders-anthropic-ban). The company that said yes got the contract; the company that said the same thing with conviction got the Huawei treatment.

